; WI-1 (NonEmptyVec): a user rule whose name equals the `NonEmpty<Elem>List` wasm wrapper that an
; inline `[+ elem]` occurrence mints must be REJECTED (never silently shadowed) — sharing the name
; would emit a wrapper of the wrong shape (loose Vec vs restricted NonEmptyVec). The collision is on
; the wasm class name, so it is graceful-rejected under --wasm=true and generates cleanly under
; --wasm=false (rust has no such wrapper: the inline field is a bare `NonEmptyVec<Bar>`).
bar = { a: uint }
non_empty_bar_list = [* bar]
holder = { tags: [+ bar] }
